message: "If you use this Project 8 study, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "When Sampled Recommendation Metrics Change Model Selection: A Reproducible Toy-Example Study"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Chegondi"
    given-names: "Keerthi Sagar"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Phoenix, Arizona, United States"
    email: "keerthisagarchegondi@gmail.com"
version: "1.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23058261"
url: "https://zenodo.org/records/23058261"
date-released: "2026-09-27"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible reconstruction and extension of a source-reported toy
  recommendation-evaluation example showing that, for fixed rank profiles,
  changing only the evaluation candidate set can change model ordering under
  Average Precision. The study includes analytical expectations, a sample-size
  sensitivity sweep, an AUC negative control, Monte Carlo checks, and
  source-value reconciliation.
keywords:
  - recommender systems
  - offline evaluation
  - negative sampling
  - average precision
  - NDCG
  - AUC
  - reproducibility
